  [PASS] V5 [statement]   THE MILKY WAY UNDER THE EQUIPARTITION LAW: with L258's own M_b = 7e10 and L240's g_ext = 2.146e-10, the zero-parameter curve gives v_c(R0) = 224 km/s (canonical) / 230 (alt) against the measured 229-235 (Eilers 229.0, Mroz 233.6, Ou ~233) -- within 5% of 232.5; the EFE line breaks at R_efe = 6.74 kpc against the registered 6.1 kpc (10%); the local dark density A/R0^2 = 0.0081-0.0089 Msun/pc^3 sits AT the measured band's lower edge and within 3-6% of the 0.0084 vertical-kinematics value, and the outer curve stays mildly declining (log-slope -0.16, non-Keplerian) exactly where the free-dust regime takes over, with the law's bracket overlapping the 1-sigma interval of every well-measured Eilers point at R >= 15 kpc and the 2-sigma interval of the noisy tail rows (mean |model-measured|/v = 3.4%).  WHAT IS NOT CLOSED: the canonical footing sits 4% low of the Eilers anchor (the registered disc-correction direction, L258 C4); the two measured pipelines disagree by ~18 km/s at 20 kpc (Eilers vs Mroz), wider than the law's bracket; raw bracket containment in the noisy tail (sigma 3-24 km/s rows at R > 20.8 kpc) is 61%; the break radius and the local-density floor become data tests at Gaia DR4 (Dec 2026); the free-dust sector's abundance is not derived (L258 A3).  The home galaxy passes the law's five checks, with the edges stated.

